    "subtopic_id": "science/grade_08/ch_02/H008",
    "stem": "Vivaan collects a drop of ditch water and a pinch of moist garden soil mixed with water. With unaided eyes he sees nothing living. Under a microscope he sees tiny moving beings and also tiny living beings that stay still.\n\nAnswer both parts.",
    "item_type": "structured",
    "options": {},
    "statements": [],
    "parts": [
      {
        "id": "i",
        "text": "Which claim correctly decides what those tiny beings are?",
        "marks": 1,
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "A",
            "text": "The tiny living beings are microorganisms, because they are living and too small for the unaided eye."
          },
          {
            "id": "B",
            "text": "A nonliving soil grain seen only under the microscope is a microorganism."
          },
          {
            "id": "C",
            "text": "Microorganisms occur only in the ditch water, not in the moist garden soil."
          }
        ]
      },
